From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:19:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] module-droid-card: announce a plugged-in jack at start-up

The previous change tells the HAL about wired headphones and headsets from
the port availability hook, which only fires on a change. The jack is read
in pa__init() before that hook is connected, so headphones that are already
plugged in when the module loads - at boot, or whenever PulseAudio is
restarted - are never announced, and a MediaTek HAL keeps dropping what is
written to them until they are pulled out and plugged in again.

Announce them once after connecting the hook. Only the wired ports, and
only when something is in the jack: droid-card leaves every other port at
its default of available, and telling the HAL that a USB or Bluetooth
device is connected would be a lie.

Seen on the Zinwa Q25 (mt6789): with headphones in at PulseAudio start,
nothing was announced and playback stayed silent until a replug; with this
change the log shows "Notifying Android of port 'output-wired_headphone'
(8) becoming available" at start-up and the headphones play.
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 src/droid/module-droid-card.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
index 38b8926..0201603 100644
--- a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
+++ b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
@@ -956,6 +956,25 @@ int pa__init(pa_module *m) {
                            PA_HOOK_NORMAL,
                            port_availability_changed_hook_callback, u);
 
+    /* The jack was read above, before this hook existed, so headphones that
+     * were already plugged in when the module loaded - at boot, or when
+     * PulseAudio restarts - have never been announced, and the HAL keeps
+     * dropping what is written to them until they are pulled and plugged in
+     * again. Announce them now. Only the wired ports, and only when something
+     * is in the jack: droid-card leaves every other port available by default,
+     * and telling the HAL a USB or Bluetooth device is connected would be a
+     * lie. */
+    {
+        pa_device_port *port;
+        void *state;
+
+        PA_HASHMAP_FOREACH(port, u->card->ports, state) {
+            if (port->available == PA_AVAILABLE_YES &&
+                pa_startswith(port->name, "output-wired_"))
+                port_availability_changed_hook_callback(NULL, port, u);
+        }
+    }
+
     pa_card_put(u->card);
 
     return 0;
